\caption(A 1×2 coarse grid expands to a 2×4 parent layout. The printed table includes all parent/previous contexts, including unseen rows left uniform by smoothing.)
\alttext(Two coloured coarse cells correspond to matching two-by-two blocks of fine cells. Each fine cell states its parent code; raster ordering continues across the fine row boundary.)

For vocabulary K=16, the actual fine prior stores 16×17×16 counts; previous=16 is BOS.
Its conditional probability is (count+0.5)/(context_total+8). A separate coarse raster Markov
prior uses previous coarse symbol/BOS. Both tables are fitted only to selected-model **fit**
codes. They are cheap first-order baselines, not PixelCNN, and cannot enforce fitting-only
provenance by themselves; the complete program chooses those inputs explicitly.

> Native local data and the complete experiment

The native beta-vae-assets task prepares the same exhaustive circle/square lattice used by
the related autoencoder reports: 294 binary 28×28 images, with 210 fit, 42 validation and
42 test factor combinations. Radius=size+2 and centre=(3x+5,3y+5); circles use inclusive
Euclidean radius and squares inclusive Chebyshev radius. Residue (x+2y+size+3shape) mod 7
assigns test=0, validation=1 and fit=2–6. Source IDs and factors are provenance only.
These small procedural teaching data are not a downloaded benchmark.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n      = dm::nn;
  const auto cache = dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("beta-vae-assets");
  const auto a     = n::load_npz((std::filesystem::path(cache) / "beta_vae/factors.npz").string());
  auto       find  = [&](const std::string& name) {
    for (const auto& [key, value] : a)
      if (key == name)
        return value;
    throw std::runtime_error(name);
  };
  std::print("| pool | records | coarse/fine tokens per image |\n|---|---:|---|\n");
  for (const std::string split : {"fit", "validation", "test"})
    std::print("| {} | {} | 49 / 196 |\n", split, find(split + "_images").size(0));
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| pool | records | coarse/fine tokens per image |
|---|---:|---|
| fit | 210 | 49 / 196 |
| validation | 42 | 49 / 196 |
| test | 42 | 49 / 196 |
// result_end

\caption(The native cache supplies all three pools. The complete program validates every source ID, factor coordinate and binary pixel against KnownFactorLattice.)

Seed 2801 creates fourteen leaves and 1,157 scalars. Encoder1=40, encoder2=148, top book=64,
top decoder=148, fine projection=36, fine book=64, decoder=584 and output=73. Leaf creation
order follows that list. The two books are independent uniform(-0.5,0.5); ReLU kernels use
He initialization, linear kernels ordinary Glorot and all biases zero.
BatchOrder(210,32,2803) gives seven batches per epoch, including eighteen final rows.
Three epochs make **21 Adam steps**, rate 0.003, moments 0.9/0.999 and epsilon 1e-8.

Every completed epoch 1–3 is eligible; validation reconstruction NLL alone selects the
checkpoint, excluding the latent penalties. A fresh model restores all fourteen leaves.
The program preserves all seventeen original saved forward fields, the first hierarchy
probe, complete batch history and both explicit prior banks. Prior fitting occurs after
selection. This is model restore, not optimizer-state resume. The actual forward, objective,
reverse mode and Adam step remain visible inside the complete loop.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
namespace nn = dm::nn;
namespace ae {
void Require(bool ok, const std::string& why) {
  if (!ok)
    throw std::runtime_error(why);
}
void Near(double a, double b, double tol, const std::string& why) {
  Require(std::abs(a - b) <= tol, why);
}
nn::Tensor Find(const nn::NamedTensors& a, const std::string& name) {
  for (const auto& [key, value] : a)
    if (key == name)
      return value;
  throw std::runtime_error(name);
}
struct BetaFactorData {
  nn::Tensor images, factors, source;
};
std::vector<BetaFactorData> LoadBetaFactors(const std::filesystem::path& root) {
  const auto arrays = nn::load_npz((root / "factors.npz").string()),
             known  = nn::models::KnownFactorLattice();
  std::vector<BetaFactorData> result;
  std::set<int>               seen;
  for (const std::string split : {"fit", "validation", "test"}) {
    const int  n   = split == "fit" ? 210 : 42;
    const auto raw = Find(arrays, split + "_images"), f = Find(arrays, split + "_factors"),
               ids = Find(arrays, split + "_source_ids");
    Require(
        raw.shape() == nn::Shape{n, 28, 28, 1} && f.shape() == nn::Shape{n, 4} &&
            f.dtype() == nn::DType::Int32 && ids.shape() == nn::Shape{n} &&
            ids.dtype() == nn::DType::Int32,
        "complete lattice schema");
    const auto                canonical_ids = Find(known, split + "_source_ids").to_vector<int>();
    std::vector<std::int64_t> rows;
    for (int id : ids.to_vector<int>()) {
      auto where = std::find(canonical_ids.begin(), canonical_ids.end(), id);
      Require(
          where != canonical_ids.end() && seen.insert(id).second,
          "unique identity in correct split");
      rows.push_back(where - canonical_ids.begin());
    }
    const auto x = nn::take_rows(Find(known, split + "_images"), rows);
    Require(
        nn::equal_bits(nn::cast(raw, nn::DType::Float32), x) &&
            nn::equal_bits(f, nn::take_rows(Find(known, split + "_factors"), rows)),
        "all factor coordinates and binary pixels match the core lattice");
    result.push_back({x, f, ids});
  }
  Require(seen.size() == 294, "exhaustive lattice");
  return result;
}
void SaveFactorData(const std::filesystem::path& root, const std::vector<BetaFactorData>& pools) {
  nn::NamedTensors arrays;
  for (int k = 0; k < 3; ++k) {
    const std::string s = k == 0 ? "fit" : k == 1 ? "validation" : "test";
    arrays.emplace_back(s + "_images", pools[k].images);
    arrays.emplace_back(s + "_factors", pools[k].factors);
    arrays.emplace_back(s + "_source_ids", pools[k].source);
  }
  nn::save_npz((root / "data.npz").string(), arrays);
}
nn::NamedTensors Arrays(const nn::ParameterStore& p) {
  nn::NamedTensors a;
  for (const auto& name : p.names())
    a.emplace_back(name, p.at(name).detach().clone());
  return a;
}
auto Snapshot(const nn::ParameterStore& p) {
  return p.flatten();
}
double VqDifference(const nn::Tensor& a, const nn::Tensor& b) {
  Require(a.shape() == b.shape(), "matching shapes");
  return nn::max(nn::abs(a - b)).item();
}
double Mse(const nn::Tensor& a, const nn::Tensor& b) {
  return nn::mean(
             nn::square(
                 nn::cast(a.reshape({a.size(0), 784}), nn::DType::Float64) -
                 nn::cast(b.reshape({b.size(0), 784}), nn::DType::Float64)))
      .item();
}
nn::Tensor PixelMean(const nn::Tensor& x) {
  return nn::cast(
      nn::mean(nn::cast(x.reshape({x.size(0), 784}), nn::DType::Float64), {0}), nn::DType::Float32);
}
nn::Tensor Constant(const nn::Tensor& row, int n) {
  return nn::broadcast_to(row.reshape({1, 784}), {n, 784}).contiguous();
}

void Warm(nn::ParameterStore& p) {
  nn::NoGradGuard guard;
  nn::models::VectorQuantizedAutoencoder2(p, nn::zeros({1, 28, 28, 1}));
}
nn::NamedTensors Evaluate(nn::ParameterStore& p, const nn::Tensor& images) {
  nn::NoGradGuard  guard;
  const auto       n = nn::models::VectorQuantizedAutoencoder2(p, images);
  nn::NamedTensors out{
      {"encoded_top", n.encoded_top},
      {"encoded_bottom", n.encoded_bottom},
      {"top_indices", n.top.indices},
      {"bottom_indices", n.bottom.indices},
      {"top_quantized", n.top.quantized},
      {"bottom_quantized", n.bottom.quantized},
      {"top_straight_through", n.top.straight_through},
      {"bottom_straight_through", n.bottom.straight_through},
      {"top_feature", n.top_feature},
      {"probability", n.probability},
      {"nll", n.nll},
      {"reconstruction_loss", n.reconstruction_loss},
      {"top_codebook_loss", n.top.codebook_loss},
      {"bottom_codebook_loss", n.bottom.codebook_loss},
      {"top_commitment_loss", n.top.commitment_loss},
      {"bottom_commitment_loss", n.bottom.commitment_loss},
      {"loss", n.loss}};
  for (auto& [name, t] : out) {
    t = t.contiguous();
    for (double v : t.to_vector<double>())
      Require(std::isfinite(v), "all VQ2 endpoints finite");
  }
  return out;
}
nn::Tensor Decode(nn::ParameterStore& p, const nn::Tensor& top, const nn::Tensor& bottom) {
  Require(
      top.dim() == 2 && bottom.dim() == 2 && top.size(0) == bottom.size(0) && top.size(1) == 49 &&
          bottom.size(1) == 196,
      "paired coarse/fine grids");
  nn::NoGradGuard guard;
  auto feature = nn::models::Vq2TopDecoder(p, nn::models::VqLookup(top, p.at("top_codebook")));
  return nn::sigmoid(
             nn::models::Vq2Decoder(
                 p, nn::models::VqLookup(bottom, p.at("bottom_codebook")), feature))
      .contiguous();
}
nn::NamedTensors HierarchyGradients(nn::ParameterStore& p, const nn::Tensor& images) {
  const auto n        = nn::models::VectorQuantizedAutoencoder2(p, images);
  const auto coupling = nn::grad(
      nn::mean(nn::square(n.encoded_bottom), {0, 1}), {n.encoded_top}, {true, false, false});
  const auto probe =
      n.reconstruction_loss + 0.0 * (nn::sum(n.top_book, {0, 1}) + nn::sum(n.bottom_book, {0, 1}));
  const auto books = nn::grad(probe, {n.top_book, n.bottom_book});
  return {
      {"bottom_encoded_square_dtop_encoded", coupling[0]},
      {"reconstruction_dtop_book", books[0]},
      {"reconstruction_dbottom_book", books[1]}};
}
nn::NamedTensors
EncodeWithTop(nn::ParameterStore& p, const nn::Tensor& images, const nn::Tensor& top) {
  nn::NoGradGuard guard;
  const auto      n = nn::models::VectorQuantizedAutoencoder2(p, images, top);
  return {{"encoded_bottom", n.encoded_bottom.contiguous()}, {"bottom_indices", n.bottom.indices}};
}
nn::NamedTensors CheckGradients(
    const nn::ParameterStore&      p,
    const std::vector<nn::Tensor>& g,
    const std::string&             finite,
    const std::string&             nonzero) {
  Require(g.size() == p.size(), "all fourteen derivative leaves");
  nn::NamedTensors out;
  const auto       names = p.names();
  for (std::size_t k = 0; k < g.size(); ++k) {
    double norm = 0;
    for (double x : g[k].to_vector<double>()) {
      Require(std::isfinite(x), finite);
      norm += x * x;
    }
    Require(norm > 0, nonzero);
    out.emplace_back(names[k], g[k]);
  }
  return out;
}
} // namespace ae
namespace check {
using ae::Near;
using ae::Require;
} // namespace check
namespace {

namespace nn = datamunge::nn;

float Scalar(const nn::NamedTensors& f, const std::string& key) {
  return ae::Find(f, key).item<float>();
}

void Run(
    const std::filesystem::path& data,
    const std::filesystem::path& root,
    int                          epochs,
    const std::string&           init) {
  auto pools = ae::LoadBetaFactors(data);
  std::filesystem::create_directories(root);
  ae::SaveFactorData(root, pools);
  nn::ParameterStore model(2801);
  ae::Warm(model);
  nn::OptimizerConfig config;
  config.kind = nn::OptimizerKind::Adam;
  nn::Optimizer optimizer(model, .003, config);
  if (!init.empty())
    model.load(init);
  check::Require(model.count() == 1157 && model.size() == 14, "compact spatial VQ census");
  nn::save_npz((root / "initial_arrays.npz").string(), ae::Arrays(model));
  nn::BatchOrder order(210, 32, 2803);
  std::ofstream  history(root / "history.tsv"), batches(root / "batches.tsv");
  history.precision(17);
  history << "epoch\ttrain_preupdate_objective\tvalidation_nll\tvalidation_top_codebook_"
             "loss\tvalidation_bottom_codebook_"
             "loss\tvalidation_top_commitment_loss\tvalidation_bottom_commitment_loss\tvalidation_"
             "objective\n";
  batches << "epoch\tstep\trow\tsource_id\n";
  const auto fit_source = pools[0].source.to_vector<int>();
  const auto best_path  = (root / "best.npz").string();
  double     best       = std::numeric_limits<double>::infinity();
  int        selected = 0, step = 0;
  const auto started = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
  for (int epoch = 1; epoch <= epochs; ++epoch) {
    order.begin_epoch();
    double sum  = 0;
    int    seen = 0;
    for (;;) {
      auto rows = order.next();
      if (rows.empty())
        break;
      auto images = nn::take_rows(pools[0].images, rows);
      if (step == 0) {
        nn::save_npz((root / "first_batch.npz").string(), {{"images", images}});
        auto g = ae::CheckGradients(
            model,
            nn::grad(
                nn::models::VectorQuantizedAutoencoder2(model, images).loss, model.parameters()),
            "all VQ gradients finite",
            "all fourteen tensors receive VQ2 gradients");
        nn::save_npz((root / "first_gradients.npz").string(), g);
        nn::save_npz((root / "first_forward.npz").string(), ae::Evaluate(model, images));
        auto   hierarchy     = ae::HierarchyGradients(model, images);
        double coupling_norm = 0;
        for (float v : ae::Find(hierarchy, "bottom_encoded_square_dtop_encoded").to_vector<float>())
          coupling_norm += std::abs(v);
        check::Require(
            coupling_norm > 0, "upper straight-through code has nonzero bottom-encoder derivative");
        for (const std::string key : {"reconstruction_dtop_book", "reconstruction_dbottom_book"})
          for (float v : ae::Find(hierarchy, key).to_vector<float>())
            check::Near(v, 0, 0, "neither codebook receives reconstruction gradients");
        nn::save_npz((root / "first_hierarchy_gradients.npz").string(), hierarchy);
      }
      const auto   forward   = nn::models::VectorQuantizedAutoencoder2(model, images);
      const double preupdate = forward.loss.item<float>();
      check::Require(std::isfinite(preupdate) && preupdate >= 0, "finite VQ2 objective");
      sum += double(rows.size()) * preupdate;
      const auto gradients = nn::grad(forward.loss, model.parameters());
      optimizer.step(gradients);
      seen += int(rows.size());
      for (auto row : rows)
        batches << epoch << '\t' << step << '\t' << row << '\t' << fit_source[row] << '\n';
      if (step == 0)
        nn::save_npz((root / "first_update_arrays.npz").string(), ae::Arrays(model));
      ++step;
    }
    check::Require(seen == 210, "all fitting cases exactly once per epoch");
    auto         validation = ae::Evaluate(model, pools[1].images);
    const double nll        = Scalar(validation, "reconstruction_loss");
    history << epoch << '\t' << sum / seen << '\t' << nll;
    for (const std::string key :
         {"top_codebook_loss",
          "bottom_codebook_loss",
          "top_commitment_loss",
          "bottom_commitment_loss",
          "loss"})
      history << '\t' << Scalar(validation, key);
    history << '\n';
    nn::save_npz(
        (root / ("epoch" + std::to_string(epoch) + "_arrays.npz")).string(), ae::Arrays(model));
    if (nll < best) {
      best     = nll;
      selected = epoch;
      model.save(best_path); // validation reconstruction NLL selects VQ checkpoint
    }
    std::cout << "epoch" << epoch << ":validation NLL=" << nll
              << ",top_dictionary=" << Scalar(validation, "top_codebook_loss")
              << ",bottom_dictionary=" << Scalar(validation, "bottom_codebook_loss") << std::endl;
  }
  const double seconds =
      std::chrono::duration<double>(std::chrono::steady_clock::now() - started).count();
  nn::ParameterStore deployed(2801);
  ae::Warm(deployed);
  deployed.load(best_path); // fresh VQ model-only restore
  check::Near(
      Scalar(ae::Evaluate(deployed, pools[1].images), "reconstruction_loss"),
      best,
      1e-8,
      "restored selected NLL");
  const auto          before = ae::Snapshot(deployed);
  nn::NamedTensors    output;
  std::vector<double> top_perplexity, bottom_perplexity;
  for (int split = 0; split < 3; ++split) {
    const std::string name = split == 0 ? "fit" : split == 1 ? "validation" : "test";
    auto              f    = ae::Evaluate(deployed, pools[split].images);
    for (const std::string level : {"top", "bottom"})
      check::Require(
          nn::equal_bits(
              ae::Find(f, level + "_straight_through"), ae::Find(f, level + "_quantized")),
          "both ST values bitexact code vectors");
    const std::int64_t n   = pools[split].images.size(0);
    auto               top = ae::Find(f, "top_indices").reshape({n, 49}).contiguous(),
         bottom            = ae::Find(f, "bottom_indices").reshape({n, 196}).contiguous();
    check::Require(
        nn::equal_bits(ae::Find(f, "probability"), ae::Decode(deployed, top, bottom)),
        "both-grid code-only decode exactly matches reconstruction");
    auto tu = nn::models::VqUsage(top), bu = nn::models::VqUsage(bottom);
    top_perplexity.push_back(tu.perplexity);
    bottom_perplexity.push_back(bu.perplexity);
    output.emplace_back(name + "_top_code_counts", tu.counts);
    output.emplace_back(name + "_bottom_code_counts", bu.counts);
    output.emplace_back(name + "_top_index_grid", top);
    output.emplace_back(name + "_bottom_index_grid", bottom);
    for (const auto& [key, value] : f)
      output.emplace_back(name + "_" + key, value);
  }
  const auto test_probability = ae::Find(output, "test_probability");
  auto       repeated         = ae::Evaluate(deployed, pools[2].images);
  check::Require(
      nn::equal_bits(ae::Find(repeated, "probability"), test_probability),
      "deterministic repeat bitexact");
  auto         single = ae::Evaluate(deployed, nn::take_rows(pools[2].images, {0}));
  const double parity =
      ae::VqDifference(ae::Find(single, "probability"), nn::take_rows(test_probability, {0}));
  check::Require(parity < 2e-6, "VQ single/batch parity");
  auto zero_top             = nn::zeros({1, 49}, nn::DType::Int32),
       one_top              = nn::full({1, 49}, 1.0, nn::DType::Int32),
       zero_bottom          = nn::zeros({1, 196}, nn::DType::Int32),
       one_bottom           = nn::full({1, 196}, 1.0, nn::DType::Int32);
  auto         zero_decoded = ae::Decode(deployed, zero_top, zero_bottom);
  const double top_effect =
                   ae::VqDifference(zero_decoded, ae::Decode(deployed, one_top, zero_bottom)),
               bottom_effect =
                   ae::VqDifference(zero_decoded, ae::Decode(deployed, zero_top, one_bottom));
  check::Require(
      top_effect > 1e-5 && bottom_effect > 1e-5, "decoder responds to BOTH discrete groups");
  auto probe_image = nn::take_rows(pools[2].images, {0});
  auto c0          = ae::EncodeWithTop(deployed, probe_image, zero_top),
       c1          = ae::EncodeWithTop(deployed, probe_image, one_top);
  const double conditioning_effect =
      ae::VqDifference(ae::Find(c0, "encoded_bottom"), ae::Find(c1, "encoded_bottom"));
  check::Require(conditioning_effect > 1e-5, "bottom encoder changes with supplied top symbols");
  nn::save_npz(
      (root / "top_conditioning_intervention.npz").string(),
      {{"images", probe_image},
       {"zero_top_encoded_bottom", ae::Find(c0, "encoded_bottom")},
       {"one_top_encoded_bottom", ae::Find(c1, "encoded_bottom")},
       {"zero_top_bottom_indices", ae::Find(c0, "bottom_indices")},
       {"one_top_bottom_indices", ae::Find(c1, "bottom_indices")}});
  for (int bad : {-1, 16}) {
    auto bad_top    = nn::full({1, 49}, double(bad), nn::DType::Int32),
         bad_bottom = nn::full({1, 196}, double(bad), nn::DType::Int32);
    for (int which = 0; which < 2; ++which) {
      bool rejected = false;
      try {
        ae::Decode(deployed, which ? zero_top : bad_top, which ? bad_bottom : zero_bottom);
      } catch (const std::exception&) {
        rejected = true;
      }
      check::Require(rejected, "invalid symbol rejected in either vocabulary");
    }
  }
  const auto fit_top     = ae::Find(output, "fit_top_index_grid"),
             fit_bottom  = ae::Find(output, "fit_bottom_index_grid"),
             test_top    = ae::Find(output, "test_top_index_grid"),
             test_bottom = ae::Find(output, "test_bottom_index_grid");
  nn::models::VqMarkovPrior       top_prior(fit_top);
  nn::models::Vq2ConditionalPrior bottom_prior(fit_top, fit_bottom);
  const auto                      top_uniform = nn::models::MidpointUniformNoise({20, 49}, 2827);
  const auto                      top_sample  = top_prior.Sample(top_uniform);
  const auto   bottom_uniform                 = nn::models::MidpointUniformNoise({20, 196}, 2833);
  const auto   bottom_sample                  = bottom_prior.Sample(top_sample, bottom_uniform);
  auto         prior_probability              = ae::Decode(deployed, top_sample, bottom_sample);
  const double prior_top_fit = top_prior.Nll(fit_top), prior_top_test = top_prior.Nll(test_top),
               prior_bottom_fit  = bottom_prior.Nll(fit_top, fit_bottom),
               prior_bottom_test = bottom_prior.Nll(test_top, test_bottom);
  nn::save_npz(
      (root / "prior.npz").string(),
      {{"top_counts", top_prior.counts()},
       {"top_probabilities", top_prior.probabilities()},
       {"bottom_counts", bottom_prior.counts()},
       {"bottom_probabilities", bottom_prior.probabilities()},
       {"sample_top_ids", top_sample},
       {"sample_bottom_ids", bottom_sample},
       {"top_uniform", top_uniform},
       {"bottom_uniform", bottom_uniform},
       {"probability", prior_probability}});

  check::Require(
      before == ae::Snapshot(deployed),
      "hierarchical prior/decoding/conditioning diagnostics preserve all parameters");
  nn::save_npz((root / "model_arrays.npz").string(), ae::Arrays(deployed));
  nn::save_npz((root / "outputs.npz").string(), output);
  const double mse      = ae::Mse(test_probability, pools[2].images);
  auto         mean     = ae::Constant(ae::PixelMean(pools[0].images), 42);
  const double mean_mse = ae::Mse(mean, pools[2].images);
  const auto   tc       = ae::Find(output, "fit_top_code_counts").to_vector<int>(),
             bc         = ae::Find(output, "fit_bottom_code_counts").to_vector<int>();
  int top_used = 0, bottom_used = 0;
  for (int k = 0; k < 16; ++k) {
    top_used += tc[k] > 0;
    bottom_used += bc[k] > 0;
  }
  const double  test_nll = Scalar(output, "test_reconstruction_loss");
  std::ofstream meta(root / "metrics.json");
  meta.precision(17);
  meta << "{\"parameters\":1157,\"tensors\":14,\"epochs\":" << epochs << ",\"updates\":" << step
       << ",\"selected_epoch\":" << selected
       << ",\"vocabulary_each\":16,\"embedding_dimensions\":4,\"top_tokens\":49,\"bottom_tokens\":"
          "196,\"commitment_"
          "beta\":0.25,\"test_nll\":"
       << test_nll << ",\"test_objective\":" << Scalar(output, "test_loss")
       << ",\"test_mse\":" << mse << ",\"fit_mean_test_mse\":" << mean_mse
       << ",\"fit_top_used\":" << top_used << ",\"fit_bottom_used\":" << bottom_used
       << ",\"fit_top_perplexity\":" << top_perplexity[0]
       << ",\"fit_bottom_perplexity\":" << bottom_perplexity[0]
       << ",\"test_top_perplexity\":" << top_perplexity[2]
       << ",\"test_bottom_perplexity\":" << bottom_perplexity[2]
       << ",\"prior_top_fit_nll\":" << prior_top_fit << ",\"prior_top_test_nll\":" << prior_top_test
       << ",\"prior_bottom_fit_nll\":" << prior_bottom_fit
       << ",\"prior_bottom_test_nll\":" << prior_bottom_test
       << ",\"single_batch_max_error\":" << parity << ",\"top_symbol_max_effect\":" << top_effect
       << ",\"bottom_symbol_max_effect\":" << bottom_effect
       << ",\"top_conditioning_bottom_encoded_max_effect\":" << conditioning_effect
       << ",\"training_seconds\":" << seconds << "}\n";
  check::Require(bool(meta) && bool(history) && bool(batches), "complete two-scale evidence");
  std::print(
      "| selected epoch | test NLL | test objective | test MSE | fit-only mean MSE | used "
      "top/bottom | fit perplexity top/bottom | prior joint test nats/grid "
      "|\n|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|---|---:|\n| {} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} | "
      "{}/{} | {:.9f}/{:.9f} | {:.9f} |\n",
      selected,
      test_nll,
      Scalar(output, "test_loss"),
      mse,
      mean_mse,
      top_used,
      bottom_used,
      top_perplexity[0],
      bottom_perplexity[0],
      prior_top_test + prior_bottom_test);
}

} // namespace

int main() {
  try {
    const std::filesystem::path cache = dm::datasets::data_home();
    dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("beta-vae-assets", cache.string());
    Run(cache / "beta_vae", "build/vq2_vae", 3, "");
    return 0;
  } catch (const std::exception& e) {
    std::cerr << e.what() << '\n';
    return 1;
  }
}
```
